      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sprang up in 1881 when the Missouri–Kansas–Texas Railroad built a depot, bypassing the earlier Brushy Mound community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/burleson-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original interurban station operated out of a drugstore, and that building now houses the Burleson Heritage Museum at the visitor center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
